# What may not enter the Docker build context.
#
# An image layer is permanent: a file copied in once is recoverable from
# `docker save` even if a later step deletes it. `.gitignore` keeps a secret out
# of *git* and has no effect here — `docker compose up --build` sends everything
# under this directory to the daemon.
#
# This is the SECOND lock; the first is the Dockerfile, which copies files by
# name and never a whole directory an operator keeps secrets in.
# tests/test_docker_build_context.py derives the secret patterns below from
# .gitignore's own secret section: add one there and this file must learn it.

# Operator secrets. deploy/age-key.txt decrypts deploy/secrets.enc.env, and with
# it DRIFTLESS_SESSION_SECRET, DRIFTLESS_API_TOKEN and POSTGRES_PASSWORD.
deploy/age-key.txt
deploy/*.key
**/*.key
backups
**/backups

# History and local state. Nothing here builds anything, and .git carries every
# secret ever committed by accident, including ones since removed from the tip.
.git
.github
.venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
.coverage
htmlcov
**/*.db
**/*.sqlite3
reports
build
dist
*.egg-info
tests
